{"surah": 65, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِىُّ إِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ ٱلنِّسَآءَ فَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ وَأَحْصُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَۖ وَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ رَبَّكُمْۖ لَا تُخْرِجُوهُنَّ مِنۢ بُيُوتِهِنَّ وَلَا يَخْرُجْنَ إِلَّآ أَن يَأْتِينَ بِفَٰحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍۚ وَتِلْكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِۚ وَمَن يَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهُۥۚ لَا تَدْرِى لَعَلَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحْدِثُ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ أَمْرًا ", "translation": "O Prophet, when you [Muslims] divorce women, divorce them for [the commencement of] their waiting period and keep count of the waiting period,[1] and fear Allāh, your Lord. Do not turn them out of their [husbands'] houses, nor should they [themselves] leave [during that period] unless they are committing a clear immorality. And those are the limits [set by] Allāh. And whoever transgresses the limits of Allāh has certainly wronged himself. You know not; perhaps Allāh will bring about after that a [different] matter.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلنَّبِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِbَّnlٱ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "طَلَّقْتُمُ", "translit": "ُmُtْqَّlَṭ", "root": "طلق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلنِّسَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَsِّnlٱ", "root": "نسو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُqِّlَṭَf", "root": "طلق"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِtَّdِʿعِl", "root": "عدد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَحْصُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُṣْḥَaʾَw", "root": "حصي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْعِدَّةَ", "translit": "َẗَّdِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عدد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَw", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "رَبَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "تُخْرِجُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُjgِrْhkُt", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بُيُوتِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِtwُyُb", "root": "بيت"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يَخْرُجْنَ", "translit": "َnْjgُrْhkَy", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يَأْتِينَ", "translit": "َnyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِفَٰحِشَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَhsِḥَٰfِb", "root": "فحش"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "مُّبَيِّنَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَnِّyَbُّm", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَتِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِtَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "حُدُودُ", "translit": "ُdwُdُḥ", "root": "حدد"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يَتَعَدَّ", "translit": "َّdَʿعَtَy", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "حُدُودَ", "translit": "َdwُdُḥ", "root": "حدد"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "فَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "ظَلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlَẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "نَفْسَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "تَدْرِى", "translit": "àِrْdَt", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "لَعَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "يُحْدِثُ", "translit": "ُhtِdْḥُy", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "بَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "أَمْرًا", "translit": "āًrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "فَإِذَا بَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ فَارِقُوهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوفٍ وَأَشْهِدُوا۟ ذَوَىْ عَدْلٍ مِّنكُمْ وَأَقِيمُوا۟ ٱلشَّهَٰدَةَ لِلَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ يُوعَظُ بِهِۦ مَن كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلْيَوْمِ ٱلْءَاخِرِۚ وَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُۥ مَخْرَجًا ", "translation": "And when they have [nearly] fulfilled their term, either retain them according to acceptable terms or part with them according to acceptable terms. And bring to witness two just men from among you and establish the testimony for [the acceptance of] Allāh. That is instructed to whoever should believe in Allāh and the Last Day. And whoever fears Allāh - He will make for him a way out[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلَغْنَ", "translit": "َnْغَlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَجَلَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَlَjgَaʾ", "root": "اجل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُkِsْmَaʾَf", "root": "مسك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِمَعْرُوفٍ", "translit": "ٍfwُrْʿعَmِb", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَارِقُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُqِrāَf", "root": "فرق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِمَعْرُوفٍ", "translit": "ٍfwُrْʿعَmِb", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَأَشْهِدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdِhْhsَaʾَw", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ذَوَىْ", "translit": "ْàَwَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَدْلٍ", "translit": "ٍlْdَʿع", "root": "عدل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّنكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُknِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَأَقِيمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmyِqَaʾَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلشَّهَٰدَةَ", "translit": "َẗَdَٰhَّhslٱ", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يُوعَظُ", "translit": "ُẓَʿعwُy", "root": "وعظ"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُ", "translit": "ُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَٱلْيَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَyْlٱَw", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِ", "translit": "ِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "يَتَّقِ", "translit": "ِqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يَجْعَل", "translit": "lَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "لَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "مَخْرَجًا", "translit": "āًjgَrْhkَm", "root": "خرج"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُۚ وَمَن يَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَهُوَ حَسْبُهُۥٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بَٰلِغُ أَمْرِهِۦۚ قَدْ جَعَلَ ٱللَّهُ لِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدْرًا ", "translation": "And will provide for him from where he does not expect. And whoever relies upon Allāh - then He is sufficient for him. Indeed, Allāh will accomplish His purpose. Allāh has already set for everything a [decreed] extent.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَرْزُقْهُ", "translit": "ُhْqُzْrَyَw", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَيْثُ", "translit": "ُhtْyَḥ", "root": "حيث"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَحْتَسِبُ", "translit": "ُbِsَtْḥَy", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَتَوَكَّلْ", "translit": "ْlَّkَwَtَy", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "حَسْبُهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhُbْsَḥ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بَٰلِغُ", "translit": "ُغِlَٰb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَمْرِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "جَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِl", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "قَدْرًا", "translit": "āًrْdَq", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَٱلَّٰٓـِٔى يَئِسْنَ مِنَ ٱلْمَحِيضِ مِن نِّسَآئِكُمْ إِنِ ٱرْتَبْتُمْ فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ ثَلَٰثَةُ أَشْهُرٍ وَٱلَّٰٓـِٔى لَمْ يَحِضْنَۚ وَأُو۟لَٰتُ ٱلْأَحْمَالِ أَجَلُهُنَّ أَن يَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّۚ وَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُۥ مِنْ أَمْرِهِۦ يُسْرًا ", "translation": "And those who no longer expect menstruation among your women - if you doubt, then their period is three months, and [also for] those who have not menstruated. And for those who are pregnant, their term is until they give birth.[1] And whoever fears Allāh - He will make for him of his matter ease.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّٰٓـِٔى", "translit": "àِٔـَّٰٓlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَئِسْنَ", "translit": "َnْsِyʾَy", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَحِيضِ", "translit": "ِḍyِḥَmْlٱ", "root": "حيض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نِّسَآئِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِyʾٓāَsِّn", "root": "نسو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنِ", "translit": "ِnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱرْتَبْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْbَtْrٱ", "root": "ريب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhُtَّdِʿعَf", "root": "عدد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ثَلَٰثَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَhtَٰlَht", "root": "ثلث"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَشْهُرٍ", "translit": "ٍrُhْhsَaʾ", "root": "شهر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَٱلَّٰٓـِٔى", "translit": "àِٔـَّٰٓlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَحِضْنَ", "translit": "َnْḍِḥَy", "root": "حيض"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَأُو۟لَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰl۟wُaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحْمَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَmْḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَجَلُهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhُlَjgَaʾ", "root": "اجل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يَضَعْنَ", "translit": "َnْʿعَḍَy", "root": "وضع"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "حَمْلَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَlْmَḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يَتَّقِ", "translit": "ِqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَجْعَل", "translit": "lَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "لَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "أَمْرِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يُسْرًا", "translit": "āًrْsُy", "root": "يسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ أَمْرُ ٱللَّهِ أَنزَلَهُۥٓ إِلَيْكُمْۚ وَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يُكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِۦ وَيُعْظِمْ لَهُۥٓ أَجْرًا ", "translation": "That is the command of Allāh, which He has sent down to you; and whoever fears Allāh - He will remove for him his misdeeds and make great for him his reward.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنزَلَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَتَّقِ", "translit": "ِqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُكَفِّرْ", "translit": "ْrِّfَkُy", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "سَيِّـَٔاتِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِtāَٔـِّyَs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَيُعْظِمْ", "translit": "ْmِẓْʿعُyَw", "root": "عظم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَجْرًا", "translit": "āًrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "أَسْكِنُوهُنَّ مِنْ حَيْثُ سَكَنتُم مِّن وُجْدِكُمْ وَلَا تُضَآرُّوهُنَّ لِتُضَيِّقُوا۟ عَلَيْهِنَّۚ وَإِن كُنَّ أُو۟لَٰتِ حَمْلٍ فَأَنفِقُوا۟ عَلَيْهِنَّ حَتَّىٰ يَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّۚ فَإِنْ أَرْضَعْنَ لَكُمْ فَـَٔاتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّۖ وَأْتَمِرُوا۟ بَيْنَكُم بِمَعْرُوفٍۖ وَإِن تَعَاسَرْتُمْ فَسَتُرْضِعُ لَهُۥٓ أُخْرَىٰ ", "translation": "Lodge them[1] [in a section] of where you dwell out of your means and do not harm them in order to oppress them.[2] And if they should be pregnant, then spend on them until they give birth. And if they breastfeed for you, then give them their payment and confer among yourselves in the acceptable way; but if you are in discord, then there may breastfeed for him [i.e., the father] another woman.[3]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَسْكِنُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُnِkْsَaʾ", "root": "سكن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَيْثُ", "translit": "ُhtْyَḥ", "root": "حيث"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَكَنتُم", "translit": "mُtnَkَs", "root": "سكن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وُجْدِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِdْjgُw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تُضَآرُّوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُّrٓāَḍُt", "root": "ضرر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لِتُضَيِّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِّyَḍُtِl", "root": "ضيق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "حَمْلٍ", "translit": "ٍlْmَḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فَأَنفِقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِfnَaʾَf", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يَضَعْنَ", "translit": "َnْʿعَḍَy", "root": "وضع"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "حَمْلَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَlْmَḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "فَإِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَرْضَعْنَ", "translit": "َnْʿعَḍْrَaʾ", "root": "رضع"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "فَـَٔاتُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُtāَٔـَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أُجُورَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَrwُjgُaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "وَأْتَمِرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrِmَtْaʾَw", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "بَيْنَكُم", "translit": "mُkَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "بِمَعْرُوفٍ", "translit": "ٍfwُrْʿعَmِb", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "تَعَاسَرْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْrَsāَʿعَt", "root": "عسر"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "فَسَتُرْضِعُ", "translit": "ُʿعِḍْrُtَsَf", "root": "رضع"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "أُخْرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrْhkُaʾ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "لِيُنفِقْ ذُو سَعَةٍ مِّن سَعَتِهِۦۖ وَمَن قُدِرَ عَلَيْهِ رِزْقُهُۥ فَلْيُنفِقْ مِمَّآ ءَاتَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُۚ لَا يُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا مَآ ءَاتَىٰهَاۚ سَيَجْعَلُ ٱللَّهُ بَعْدَ عُسْرٍ يُسْرًا ", "translation": "Let a man of wealth spend from his wealth, and he whose provision is restricted - let him spend from what Allāh has given him. Allāh does not charge a soul except [according to] what He has given it. Allāh will bring about, after hardship, ease [i.e., relief].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِيُنفِقْ", "translit": "ْqِfnُyِl", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذُو", "translit": "wُhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَعَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَʿعَs", "root": "وسع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَعَتِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِtَʿعَs", "root": "وسع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قُدِرَ", "translit": "َrِdُq", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رِزْقُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُqْzِr", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَلْيُنفِقْ", "translit": "ْqِfnُyْlَf", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ءَاتَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُكَلِّفُ", "translit": "ُfِّlَkُy", "root": "كلف"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "نَفْسًا", "translit": "āًsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ءَاتَىٰهَا", "translit": "āَhٰàَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "سَيَجْعَلُ", "translit": "ُlَʿعْjgَyَs", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "عُسْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْsُʿع", "root": "عسر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "يُسْرًا", "translit": "āًrْsُy", "root": "يسر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَكَأَيِّن مِّن قَرْيَةٍ عَتَتْ عَنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّهَا وَرُسُلِهِۦ فَحَاسَبْنَٰهَا حِسَابًا شَدِيدًا وَعَذَّبْنَٰهَا عَذَابًا نُّكْرًا ", "translation": "And how many a city was insolent toward the command of its Lord and His messengers, so We took it to severe account and punished it with a terrible punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَأَيِّن", "translit": "nِّyَaʾَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَرْيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyْrَq", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَتَتْ", "translit": "ْtَtَʿع", "root": "عتو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَنْ", "translit": "ْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَمْرِ", "translit": "ِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَبِّهَا", "translit": "āَhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَرُسُلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlُsُrَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَحَاسَبْنَٰهَا", "translit": "āَhَٰnْbَsāَḥَf", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حِسَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَsِḥ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "شَدِيدًا", "translit": "āًdyِdَhs", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَعَذَّبْنَٰهَا", "translit": "āَhَٰnْbَّhdَʿعَw", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَذَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "نُّكْرًا", "translit": "āًrْkُّn", "root": "نكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "فَذَاقَتْ وَبَالَ أَمْرِهَا وَكَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ أَمْرِهَا خُسْرًا ", "translation": "And it tasted the bad consequence of its affair [i.e., rebellion], and the outcome of its affair was loss.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَذَاقَتْ", "translit": "ْtَqāَhdَf", "root": "ذوق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَبَالَ", "translit": "َlāَbَw", "root": "وبل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَمْرِهَا", "translit": "āَhِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَكَانَ", "translit": "َnāَkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَٰقِبَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَbِqَٰʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَمْرِهَا", "translit": "āَhِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خُسْرًا", "translit": "āًrْsُhk", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "أَعَدَّ ٱللَّهُ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيدًاۖ فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ يَٰٓأُو۟لِى ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ۚ قَدْ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيْكُمْ ذِكْرًا ", "translation": "Allāh has prepared for them a severe punishment; so fear Allāh, O you of understanding who have believed. Allāh has sent down to you a message [i.e., the Qur’ān].[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَعَدَّ", "translit": "َّdَʿعَaʾ", "root": "عدد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَذَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "شَدِيدًا", "translit": "āًdyِdَhs", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَٰٓأُو۟لِى", "translit": "àِl۟wُaʾَٰٓy", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰbْlَaʾْlٱ", "root": "لبب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَنزَلَ", "translit": "َlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ذِكْرًا", "translit": "āًrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "رَّسُولًا يَتْلُوا۟ عَلَيْكُمْ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ مُبَيِّنَٰتٍ لِّيُخْرِجَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۚ وَمَن يُؤْمِنۢ بِٱللَّهِ وَيَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا يُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّٰتٍ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدًاۖ قَدْ أَحْسَنَ ٱللَّهُ لَهُۥ رِزْقًا ", "translation": "[He sent] a Messenger [i.e., Muḥammad (ﷺ)] reciting to you the distinct verses of Allāh that He may bring out those who believe and do righteous deeds from darknesses into the light. And whoever believes in Allāh and does righteousness - He will admit him into gardens beneath which rivers flow to abide therein forever. Allāh will have perfected for him a provision.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَّسُولًا", "translit": "āًlwُsَّr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَتْلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlْtَy", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُبَيِّنَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰnِّyَbُm", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِّيُخْرِجَ", "translit": "َjgِrْhkُyِّl", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰmُlُّẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلنُّورِ", "translit": "ِrwُّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَيَعْمَلْ", "translit": "ْlَmْʿعَyَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "صَٰلِحًا", "translit": "āًḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يُدْخِلْهُ", "translit": "ُhْlِhkْdُy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "تَجْرِى", "translit": "àِrْjgَt", "root": "جري"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "تَحْتِهَا", "translit": "āَhِtْḥَt", "root": "تحت"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ", "translit": "ُrَٰhْnَaʾْlٱ", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "خَٰلِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِlَٰhk", "root": "خلد"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "فِيهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbَaʾ", "root": "ابد"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "رِزْقًا", "translit": "āًqْzِr", "root": "رزق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَٰوَٰتٍ وَمِنَ ٱلْأَرْضِ مِثْلَهُنَّ يَتَنَزَّلُ ٱلْأَمْرُ بَيْنَهُنَّ لِتَعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَدْ أَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًۢا ", "translation": "It is Allāh who has created seven heavens and of the earth, the like of them.[1] [His] command descends among them so you may know that Allāh is over all things competent and that Allāh has encompassed all things in knowledge.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَلَقَ", "translit": "َqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَبْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَمَٰوَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰwَٰmَs", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِثْلَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَlْhtِm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَتَنَزَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّzَnَtَy", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لِتَعْلَمُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُmَlْʿعَtِl", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "قَدِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِdَq", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "أَحَاطَ", "translit": "َṭāَḥَaʾ", "root": "حوط"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِb", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عِلْمًۢا", "translit": "āًۢmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "ولذلك قال الله تعالى: ﴿ ومن يتعد حدود الله فقد ظلم نفسه ﴾ {} ولأن أصول هذه المعانى لا تختلف فيها الشرائع وإنما تختلف في وجوه التحديد كما يحد شرع عيسى ابن مريم عليه السلام تحريم الخمر بالسكر وقد حده شرعنا بكونه من جنس المسكر لأن قليله يدعو إلى كثير والداخل في الحدود داخل في التحريم بحكم الجنس كما دخل أصل المعنى بالجملة الأصلية فهذا مثال واحد لحكمه خفية من حكم النقدين فينبغى أن يعتبر شكر النعمة وكفرانها بهذا المثال فكل ما خلق لحكمة فينبغى أن يصرف عنها ولا يعرف هذا إلا من قد عرف الحكمة - ومن يؤت ال", "english": "Therefore, Allah the Exalted said: 'And whoever transgresses the boundaries (hudud) of Allah has indeed wronged his own soul (nafs).' {} Because the foundations of these meanings do not differ among the divine laws (shara'i'), but they differ in the aspects of specification (tahdid), just as the law (shar') of Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him, specified the prohibition of wine (khamr) by intoxication (sukr), while our law (shar') specified it by being of the intoxicating kind (jins al-muskir) because a little of it leads to much. And what falls within the boundaries (hudud) falls within the prohibition by the ruling of the kind (jins), just as the original meaning entered in the original totality. This is one example of its hidden ruling from the ruling of the two currencies. Therefore, one should consider gratitude (shukr) for the blessing (ni'mah) and ingratitude (kufran) with this example, for everything created for a wisdom (hikmah) should be directed away from it, and none knows this except one who has known the wisdom (hikmah) - 'And whoever is given wisdom (hikmah) has been given much good' - but the jewels of wisdom (hikmah) do not encounter hearts (qulub) that are dunghills of desires (shahawat) and playgrounds of devils (shayatin); rather, none remember except those of understanding (ulu al-albab). And therefore, He said: 'Were it not that the devils (shayatin) hover around the hearts (qulub) of the children of Adam, they would look at the dominion (malakut) of the heavens.' And when you have known this example, then measure against it your movement and stillness, your speech and silence, and every action issuing from you, for it is either gratitude (shukr) or ingratitude (kufr), as it is inconceivable to be free from them. And some of that is described in the language of jurisprudence (fiqh) that the common people speak with as disliked (makruh) and some as dangerous (khatr), and all of that is described as dangerous (khatr) by the possessors of hearts (arbab al-qulub).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ولكل واحد من ذلك حدود لابد من مراعاتها بدوام المراقبة ومن يتعد حدود الله فقد ظلم نفسه فينبغي أن يتفقد العبد نفسه في جميع أوقاته في هذه الأقسام الثلاثة", "english": "And for each one of these there are limits that must be observed through constant vigilance (Muraqaba), and whoever transgresses the limits of Allah has wronged his own soul (Nafs). Therefore, the servant (Abd) should examine himself in all his times within these three divisions.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monitoring and Accounting", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monitoring and Accounting'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الثاني عشر في الطلاق وليعلم أنه مباح ولكنه أبغض المباحات إلى الله تعالى وإنما يكون مباحا إذا لم يكن فيه إيذاء بالباطل ومهما طلقها فقد آذاها ولا يباح إيذاء الغير إلا بجناية من جانبها أو بضرورة من جانبه قال الله تعالى (فإن أطعنكم فلا تبغوا عليهن سبيلا) أي لا تطلبوا حيلة للفراق وإن كرهها أبوه فليطلقها قال ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما كان تحتي امرأة أحبها وكان أبي يكرهها ويأمرني بطلاقها فراجعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال يا ابن عمر طلق امرأتك فهذا يدل على أن حق الوالد مقدم ولكن والد يكرهها لا لغرض ف", "english": "The twelfth [chapter] is on divorce, and it should be known that it is permissible but it is the most detested of permissible things to Allah the Exalted. It is only permissible if there is no harm without right, and whenever he divorces her, he has harmed her. It is not permissible to harm others except due to a transgression from her side or a necessity from his side. Allah the Exalted said: (Then if they obey you, do not seek a way against them) meaning do not seek a stratagem for separation. And if her father dislikes her, let him divorce her. Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her and ordered me to divorce her, so I consulted the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: O Ibn Umar, divorce your wife. This indicates that the right of the parent takes precedence, but a parent who dislikes her without a corrupt purpose like Umar. And whenever she harms her husband and is insolent toward his family, she is a transgressor. Likewise, if she is of bad character or corrupt in religion. Ibn Mas'ud said regarding His statement, the Exalted: 'nor should they leave except that they commit a clear immorality' - whenever she is insolent toward his family and harms her husband, that is an immorality. This is intended for the waiting period, but it is an indication of the intended meaning. And if the harm is from the husband, she may ransom herself by giving wealth; it is disliked for the man to take from her more than what he gave, for that is injustice against her and oppression upon her and trading on the private part. He, the Exalted, said: 'Then there is no blame upon them for what she gives back.' So returning what he took or less is suitable for the ransom. If she asks for divorce without any wrongdoing, she is sinful. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: (Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any wrongdoing will not smell the fragrance of Paradise). In another wording: 'Paradise is forbidden to her.' And in another wording: He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: (The women who seek khul' are the hypocrites). Then the husband should observe four matters in divorce: The first is that he divorce her in a state of purity in which he has not had intercourse with her, for divorce during menstruation or the purity in which he had intercourse is called forbidden, even if it occurs, due to what it contains of prolonging the waiting period upon her. If he does that, let him take her back. Ibn Umar divorced his wife during menstruation, so He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Umar: Command him to take her back until she becomes pure, then she menstruates, then she becomes pure, then if he wishes, he divorces her, and if he wishes, he retains her. That is the waiting period which Allah commanded to divorce women for. And He commanded him to be patient after taking her back for two purity periods so that the purpose of taking back is not...", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k02.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Marriage", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Etiquette of Marriage'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "2": [{"arabic": "الثالثة: أن ينظر فيما يأخذه فإن لم يكن من حل تورع عنه ومن يتق الله يجعل له مخرجا ويرزقه من حيث لا يحتسب ولن يعدم المتورع عن الحرام فتوحا من الحلال فلا يأخذ من أموال الأتراك والجنود وعمال السلاطين ومن أكثر كسبه من الحرام إلا إذا ضاق الأمر عليه وكان ما يسلم إليه لا يعرف له مالكا معينا فله أن يأخذ بقدر الحاجة فإن فتوى الشرع في مثل هذا أن يتصدق به على ما سيأتي بيانه في كتاب الحلال والحرام وذلك إذا عجز عن الحلال فإذا أخذ لم يكن أخذه أخذ زكاة إذ لا يقع زكاة عن مؤديه وهو حرام.", "english": "The third: That he looks at what he takes; if it is not from lawful (Halal) sources, he should abstain from it. And whoever is God-fearing (Yattaqi Allah) [i.e., practices God-consciousness (Taqwa)], He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect. And the one who abstains from the forbidden (Haram) will not lack openings from the lawful (Halal). So he should not take from the wealth of the Turks, soldiers, and the agents of sultans, and from those whose earnings are mostly from the forbidden (Haram), except when the matter becomes tight for him and what is handed to him has no known specific owner; then he may take according to need. For the legal ruling (Fatwa) in such a case is that he should give it in charity (Tasaddaqa), as will be explained in the book of the lawful (Halal) and the forbidden (Haram). And that is when he is unable to find lawful (Halal) means. If he takes it, his taking is not considered taking of alms (Zakat), since alms (Zakat) does not apply to one who gives it, and it is forbidden (Haram).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Zakat", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Mysteries of Zakat'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فإذن عليك بالقناعة بالنزر القليل والرضا بالقوت فإنه يأتيك لا محالة وإن فررت منه، وعند ذلك على الله أن يبعث إليك رزقك على يدي من لا تحتسب، فإن اشتغلت بالتقوى شاهدت بالتجربة مصداق قوله تعالى: \" ومن يتق الله يجعل له مخرجاً ويرزقه من حيث لا يحتسب \" الآية، إلا أنه لم يتكفل له أن يرزقه لحم الطير ولذائذ الأطعمة، فما ضمن إلا الرزق الذي تدوم به حياته، وهذا المضمون مبذول كل من اشتغل بالضامن واطمأن إلى ضمانه؛ فإن الذي أحاط به تدبير الله من الأسباب الخفية للرزق أعظم مما ظهر للخلق، بل مداخل الرزق لا تحصى ومج", "english": "Therefore, upon you is contentment with the little amount and satisfaction with the sustenance, for it will come to you inevitably even if you flee from it, and at that point, it is upon Allah to send to you your provision at the hands of one you do not expect. If you occupy yourself with God-consciousness (Taqwa), you will witness through experience the truth of His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever is conscious of Allah (Yattaqi Allah), He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect' (Quran 65:2-3), except that He has not guaranteed to provide him with the meat of birds and delights of foods, but only guaranteed the provision by which his life continues, and this guarantee is granted to everyone who occupies themselves with the Guarantor and is reassured by His guarantee; for what encompasses it from the hidden causes of provision by the arrangement of Allah is greater than what has appeared to creation, indeed the entrances of provision cannot be counted and its channels cannot be guided to, and that is because its appearance is on earth and its cause is in the heaven, Allah the Exalted said: 'And in the heaven is your provision and what you are promised' (Quran 51:22), and the secrets of the heaven are not disclosed, and for this reason a group entered upon Al-Junayd and he said: What do you seek? They said: We seek provision. He said: If you know in which place it is, then seek it. They said: We ask Allah. He said: If you know that He forgets you, then remind Him. They said: We enter the house and rely (Natawakkal) and see what will be. He said: Reliance (Tawakkul) based on experience is doubt. They said: So what is the remedy? He said: Abandoning the remedy.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ق  الجوار  اعلم  أن الجوار يقضي حقا وراء ما تقتضيه أخوة الإسلام فيستحق الجار  المسلم  ما  يستحقه كل مسلم وزيادة إذ قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم الجيران ثلاثة جار له حق  واحد وجار له حقان وجار له ثلاثة حقوق فالجار الذي له ثلاثة حقوق  الجار  المسلم  ذو الرحم فله حق الجوار وحق الإسلام وحق الرحم وأما الذي له  حقان  فالجار  المسلم له حق الجوار وحق الإسلام وأما الذي له حق واحد  فالجار  المشرك  حديث  الجيران ثلاثة جار له حق وجار له حقان وجار له ثلاثة حقوق الحديث أخرجه الحسن بن  سفيان والبزار في مسنديهم", "english": "Chapter on Neighbors. Know that neighborliness imposes a right beyond what the brotherhood of Islam requires, so the Muslim neighbor deserves what every Muslim deserves and more, for the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Neighbors are three: a neighbor with one right, a neighbor with two rights, and a neighbor with three rights. The neighbor with three rights is the Muslim neighbor who is a relative, so he has the right of neighborliness, the right of Islam, and the right of kinship. As for the one with two rights, it is the Muslim neighbor who has the right of neighborliness and the right of Islam. As for the one with one right, it is the polytheist neighbor.' The hadith 'Neighbors are three: a neighbor with one right, a neighbor with two rights, and a neighbor with three rights' was reported by Al-Hasan bin Sufyan and Al-Bazzar in their Musnads, Abu Al-Sheikh in Kitab Al-Thawab, and Abu Nu'aym in Al-Hilyah from the narration of Jabir, and Ibn 'Adi from the narration of 'Abdullah bin 'Umar, and both are weak. See how he affirmed a right for the polytheist merely due to neighborliness. And he (peace be upon him) said: 'Be the best neighbor to whoever neighbors you, and you will be a Muslim.' The hadith 'Be the best neighbor to whoever neighbors you, and you will be a Muslim' was mentioned earlier. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Jibril kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.' The hadith 'Jibril kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir' is agreed upon from the narration of 'A'ishah and Ibn 'Umar. And he (peace be upon him) said: 'Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor.' The hadith 'Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor' is agreed upon from the narration of Abu Shuraih. And he (peace be upon him) said: 'A servant does not believe until his neighbor is safe from his harms.' The hadith 'A servant does not believe until his neighbor is safe from his harms' was reported by Al-Bukhari from the narration of Abu Shuraih as well. And he (peace be upon him) said: 'The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.' The hadith 'The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors' was reported by Ahmad and Al-Tabarani from the narration of 'Uqbah bin 'Amir with a weak chain. And he (peace be upon him) said: 'If you throw a stone at your neighbor's dog, you have harmed him.' The hadith 'If you throw a stone at your neighbor's dog, you have harmed him' I did not find a source for. And it is narrated that a man came to Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and said to him: 'I have a neighbor who harms me, insults me, and makes things difficult for me.' He said: 'Go, and if he disobeys Allah regarding you, then obey Allah regarding him.' And it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): 'So-and-so woman fasts during the day and prays at night, but she harms her neighbors.' He said: 'She is in the Fire.' The hadith 'So-and-so woman fasts during the day and prays at night, but she harms her neighbors, so he said: She is in the Fire' was reported by Ahmad and Al-Hakim from the narration of Abu Hurairah, and he said its chain is authentic. And a man came to him (peace be upon him) complaining about his neighbor, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: 'Be patient.' Then he said to him on the third or fourth time: 'Put your belongings in the road.' He said: So people passed by him and said: 'What is this?'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k05.doc.txt", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "وقال الله تعالى ومن يتق الله يجعل له مخرجا من الإشكالات والشبه ويرزقه من حيث لا يحتسب يعلمه علما من غير تعلم ويفطنه من غير تجربة", "english": "And Allah the Exalted said: 'And whoever is God-fearing (Yattaqi Allah) makes for him a way out from the difficulties and doubts, and provides for him from where he does not reckon, teaches him knowledge without learning, and makes him discerning without experience.'", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "General"}, {"arabic": "ولا ينفك الإنسان عن الحرص إلا بحسن ثقته بتدبير الله تعالى في تقدير أرزاق العباد، وأن ذلك يحصل لا محالة مع الإجمال في الطلب، بل ينبغي أن يعلم أن رزق الله للعبد من حيث لا يحتسب أكثر قال الله تعالى \"ومن يتق الله يجعل له مخرجاً ويرزقه من حيث لا يحتسب\" فإذا انسد عليه الباب كان ينتظر الرزق منه فلا ينبغي أن يضطرب قلبه لأجله، وقال ﷺ \"أبى الله أن يرزق عبده المؤمن إلا من حيث لا يحتسب\"[44] وقال سفيان: اتق الله فما رأيت تقياً محتاجاً. أي لا يترك التقى فاقداً لضرورته، بل يلقى الله في قلوب المسلمين أن يوصلوا ", "english": "And the human being does not break free from greed except through good trust in the arrangement (tadbir) of Allah the Exalted in the apportioning of the provisions (arzaq) of the servants, and that this occurs inevitably with moderation in seeking. Rather, it is necessary to know that the provision (rizq) of Allah for the servant from where he does not reckon is greater. Allah the Exalted said: \"And whoever is God-fearing (yattaqi) Allah, He makes for him a way out and provides for him from where he does not reckon.\" So if the door is closed upon him, he should expect the provision (rizq) from it, and it is not appropriate for his heart (qalb) to be agitated because of it. And the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah refuses to provide for His believing servant except from where he does not reckon.\" And Sufyan said: Be God-fearing (ittaqi) Allah, for I have not seen a God-fearing (taqiyyan) person in need. Meaning, He does not leave the God-fearing (taqwa) one lacking his necessity, but rather Allah casts into the hearts (qulub) of the Muslims that they convey to him his provision (rizq).", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-7a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Miserliness and Love of Wealth", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Condemnation of Miserliness and Love of Wealth'", "badge": "Insight"}], "3": [{"arabic": "شاة المسمومة رواه أبو داود من حديث جابر وفيه انقطاع وحديث أنه دمى\n     وجهه وكسرت رباعيته متفق عليه من حديث سهل بن سعد في غزوة أحد وحديث اللهم\n   اغفر لقومي فإنهم لا يعلمون رواه البيهقي في دلائل النبوة والحديث في الصحيح\n   من حديث ابن مسعود أنه ﭬ حكاه عن نبي من الأنبياء ضربه قومه وحديث لبس الصوف\n  رواه الطيالسي من حديث سهل بن سعد وحديث ركوبه الحمار وإردافه خلفه متفق عليه\n      من حديث أسامة بن زيد وحديث وضع طعامه بالأرض رواه أحمد في الزهد من حديث\n  الحسن مرسلا وللبخاري من حديث أنس ما أكل رسول ال", "english": "[109] Hadith: Whoever increases in seeking forgiveness (Istighfar), Allah makes for him from every distress a relief and from every grief an exit, and provides for him from where he does not reckon. Reported by Abu Dawud, al-Nasa'i in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah, Ibn Majah, and al-Hakim, who said its chain is authentic (Sahih al-Isnad) from the narration of Ibn 'Abbas, and Ibn Hibban weakened it.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication", "badge": "Hadith"}], "7": [{"arabic": "ومن كان غرضه الرفق وطلب الثواب به فله أن يستقرض على حسن الظن بالله لا على اعتماد السلاطين الظلمة، فإن رزقه الله من حلال قضاه. وغن مات قبل القضاء قضاه الله تعالى عنه وأرضى غرماءه، وذلك بشرط أن يكون مكشوف الحال عند من يقرضه فلا يغر المقرض ولا يخدعه بالمواعيد بل يكشف حاله عنده ليقدم على إقراضه على بصيرة، ودين مثل هذا الرجل واجب أن يقضى من مال بيت المال ومن الزكاة، وقد قال تعالى: \" ومن قدر عليه رزقه فلينفق مما آتاه الله \" قيل معناه: ليبع أحد ثوبيه. وقيل معناه: فليستقرض بجاهه، فذلك مما آتاه الله. وقا", "english": "And whoever intends kindness and seeks reward through it, he may borrow based on good expectation (husn al-zann) of Allah, not relying on oppressive rulers. If Allah provides him from lawful means, he repays it. And if he dies before repayment, Allah repays it on his behalf and satisfies his creditors, provided that his situation is disclosed to the one who lends to him, so he does not deceive the lender nor trick him with promises, but reveals his situation to him so that he proceeds with lending with insight. The debt of such a man is obligatory to be repaid from the treasury (bayt al-mal) and from alms (zakah). And Allah the Exalted said: \"And whoever is constrained in his provision, let him spend from what Allah has given him.\" It is said its meaning: let him sell one of his two garments. And it is said its meaning: let him borrow through his status, for that is from what Allah has given him. And some of them said: Verily, Allah the Exalted has servants who spend according to the measure of their goods, and Allah has servants who spend according to the measure of good expectation (husn al-zann) of Allah the Exalted.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}], "11": [{"arabic": "الحمد لله الذي بيده مقاليد الأمور، وبقدرته مفاتيح الخيرات والشرور، مخرج أوليائه من الظلمات إلى النور، ومورد أعدائه ورطات الغرور، والصلاة على محمد مخرج الخلائق من الديجور، وعلى آله وأصحابه الذين لم تغرهم الحياة الدنيا ولم يغرهم بالله الغرور، صلاة تتوالى على ممر الدهور ومكر الساعات والشهور. أما بعد: فمفتاح السعادة التيقظ والفطنة، ومنبع الشقاوة الغرور والغفلة فلا نعمة لله على عباده أعظم من الإيمان والمعرفة، ولا وسيلة سوى انشراح الصدر بنور البصيرة، ولا نقمة أعظم من الكفر والمعصية، ولا داعي إليهما سو", "english": "Praise be to Allah who in His hand are the keys of affairs, and by His power are the keys of good and evil, who brings out His allies from the darknesses to the light, and brings His enemies into the pits of delusion, and prayers upon Muhammad, the bringer out of creation from the darkness, and upon his family and companions who were not deluded by the worldly life and were not deluded about Allah by delusion, prayers that continue through the passage of ages and the plotting of hours and months. After: The key to happiness is vigilance and insight, and the source of misery is delusion and heedlessness, so there is no blessing from Allah upon His servants greater than faith and knowledge, and no means except the expansion of the chest with the light of insight, and no punishment greater than disbelief and disobedience, and no caller to them except the blindness of the heart with the darkness of ignorance. The intelligent ones and possessors of insights, their hearts are \"like a niche containing a lamp, the lamp in a glass, the glass as if it were a brilliant star, lit from a blessed olive tree, neither of the east nor of the west, whose oil would almost glow even if untouched by fire - light upon light\" (Quran 24:35). And the deluded ones, their hearts are \"like darknesses in a deep sea covered by waves, upon which are waves, above which are clouds - darknesses, one above another. If one stretches out his hand, he can hardly see it. And he for whom Allah has not made light - for him there is no light\" (Quran 24:40). The intelligent ones are those whom Allah intended to guide, so He expanded their chests for Islam and guidance. And the deluded ones are those whom Allah intended to misguide, so He made their chests tight and constricted as if they were climbing into the sky. And the deluded person is the one whose insight has not opened to be sufficient for the guidance of his soul and", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-10a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "12": [{"arabic": "ما شاء الله كان وما لم يشأ لم يكن أعلم أن الله على كل شيء قدير وأن الله قد أحاط بكل شيء علما وأحصى كل شيء عددا اللهم إني أعوذ بك من شر نفسي ومن شر كل دابة أنت آخذ بناصيتها إن ربي على صراط مستقيم[134]", "english": "What Allah wills happens, and what He does not will does not happen. I know that Allah is over every thing powerful (Qadir) and that Allah has encompassed every thing in knowledge ('Ilm) and has counted every thing in number. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul (Nafs) and from the evil of every creature You take by its forelock. Indeed, my Lord is on a straight path (Sirat Mustaqim).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 3220], [2, 3220, 5254], [3, 5254, 6330], [4, 6330, 8137], [5, 8137, 10843], [6, 10843, 13629], [7, 13629, 15918], [8, 15918, 18180], [9, 18180, 19573], [10, 19573, 21738], [11, 21738, 22828], [12, 22828, 24138], [13, 24138, 24855], [14, 24855, 27324], [15, 27324, 27876], [16, 27876, 30179], [17, 30179, 31310], [18, 31310, 32924], [19, 32924, 34885], [20, 34885, 35492], [21, 35492, 37202], [22, 37202, 38774], [23, 38774, 40946], [24, 40946, 42187], [25, 42187, 43456], [26, 43456, 44546], [27, 44546, 45511], [28, 45511, 47014], [29, 47014, 48283], [30, 48283, 49373], [31, 49373, 50325], [32, 50325, 51235], [33, 51235, 52338], [34, 52338, 53055], [35, 53055, 54365], [36, 54365, 55455], [37, 55455, 56545], [38, 56545, 57841], [39, 57841, 58724], [40, 58724, 59761], [41, 59761, 61085]], "2": [[1, 400, 1701], [2, 1701, 2790], [3, 2790, 4530], [4, 4530, 7226], [5, 7226, 9006], [6, 9006, 9723], [7, 9723, 12286], [8, 12286, 14066], [9, 14066, 16430], [10, 16430, 17519], [11, 17519, 18435], [12, 18435, 19883], [13, 19883, 22406], [14, 22406, 24170], [15, 24170, 25139], [16, 25139, 26403], [17, 26403, 27864], [18, 27864, 28369], [19, 28369, 28900], [20, 28900, 29856], [21, 29856, 31131], [22, 31131, 32446], [23, 32446, 34252], [24, 34252, 35793], [25, 35793, 36723], [26, 36723, 37905], [27, 37905, 38954], [28, 38954, 40269], [29, 40269, 40973], [30, 40973, 42486]], "3": [[1, 400, 2402], [2, 2402, 2943], [3, 2943, 3944], [4, 3944, 4648], [5, 4648, 6190], [6, 6190, 7137], [7, 7137, 8964], [8, 8964, 9965], [9, 9965, 11034], [10, 11034, 11954], [11, 11954, 13453], [12, 13453, 14441], [13, 14441, 15510], [14, 15510, 16511], [15, 16511, 17620], [16, 17620, 18283], [17, 18283, 19149], [18, 19149, 20218], [19, 20218, 21233], [20, 21233, 22180], [21, 22180, 23547]], "4": [[1, 400, 2747], [2, 2747, 4158], [3, 4158, 4734], [4, 4734, 6519], [5, 6519, 7095], [6, 7095, 10265], [7, 10265, 10898], [8, 10898, 12496], [9, 12496, 14886], [10, 14886, 16211], [11, 16211, 17449], [12, 17449, 19796], [13, 19796, 20372], [14, 20372, 21783], [15, 21783, 23741], [16, 23741, 25814], [17, 25814, 27700], [18, 27700, 28333], [19, 28333, 29773], [20, 29773, 31630], [21, 31630, 32638], [22, 32638, 33919], [23, 33919, 35056], [24, 35056, 36481], [25, 36481, 37244], [26, 37244, 37820], [27, 37820, 39001], [28, 39001, 40500]], "5": [[1, 400, 1510], [2, 1510, 2455], [3, 2455, 3622], [4, 3622, 5554], [5, 5554, 7237], [6, 7237, 8271], [7, 8271, 9585], [8, 9585, 10752], [9, 10752, 12303], [10, 12303, 13219], [11, 13219, 15441], [12, 15441, 17361], [13, 17361, 18347], [14, 18347, 19838]], "6": [[1, 400, 3107], [2, 3107, 3699], [3, 3699, 4794], [4, 4794, 6303], [5, 6303, 7324], [6, 7324, 9025], [7, 9025, 10238], [8, 10238, 14102], [9, 14102, 17127], [10, 17127, 19213], [11, 19213, 20308], [12, 20308, 21329], [13, 21329, 22897], [14, 22897, 23814], [15, 23814, 26329], [16, 26329, 28415], [17, 28415, 29968], [18, 29968, 31447], [19, 31447, 33355], [20, 33355, 34302], [21, 34302, 35989], [22, 35989, 36877], [23, 36877, 39466], [24, 39466, 41848], [25, 41848, 44452], [26, 44452, 46079], [27, 46079, 48061], [28, 48061, 49156], [29, 49156, 51493], [30, 51493, 53446], [31, 53446, 54434], [32, 54434, 56122]], "7": [[1, 400, 2140], [2, 2140, 2894], [3, 2894, 3793], [4, 3793, 4793], [5, 4793, 6011], [6, 6011, 7026], [7, 7026, 7954], [8, 7954, 9288], [9, 9288, 1